WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.520
Every year on 21 June, the world
marks the International Day of Yoga.

2
00:00:05.570 --> 00:00:08.060
It was first held in 2015.

3
00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:13.030
In many gyms, yoga means fitness,
flexibility and stress relief.

4
00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:16.630
Yet the classic early text
on yoga, the Yoga Sutras,

5
00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:19.130
says very little about postures.

6
00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:24.800
So is gym yoga the same yoga that Hindu
teachers practised to win liberation?

7
00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:28.640
In this mission, you'll climb the
eight limbs of Patanjali's yoga,

8
00:00:28.690 --> 00:00:30.280
rung by rung.

9
00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:35.610
Then you'll trace yoga's journey west,
from a speech in Chicago in 1893 to the

10
00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:37.200
gyms of today.

11
00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:42.610
Your mission: find out how the yoga of the
gym connects to the yoga of liberation.
